From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:30:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Name the PMP report on the PMP

The GPU and the DCP send their power votes through the retained PMP.
Before each vote, the PMP owner waits until the PMP report says the PMP
is running (apple_pmp_report_wait_supplier_ready()). On the J604 the
PMP had no apple,pmp-report and the report node stayed disabled, so the
wait fell through to the T6030 path and returned -ENODEV. The 10.1 boot
showed the result:

  asahi: PMP AGX vote failed: -19

Enable the report and name it on the PMP, as t8132-j713.dts and
t8132-j713-gpu.dtsi do for the J713. The report window is at the same
place in the J604 ADT (pmgr reg[41], mcc reg[9]) as on the J713. The
T8132 report driver only reads it.

Fixes: ac4e9ecec6 ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Hand the PMP to Linux")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi | 5 +++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts      | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
index a53e6b2791..60ee2d8a55 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
@@ -102,6 +102,11 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/* The existing report provider owns readiness for shared PMP commands. */
+&pmp {
+	apple,pmp-report = <&pmp_report>;
+};
+
 /* The outer TVM gate is the parent of the GFX PMGR domain, as on J713. */
 &ps_gfx {
 	status = "okay";
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 9708724549..290674fc37 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -703,6 +703,14 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The PMP report (0x3803c0000 + 0x20000) lies in the J604 ADT pmgr reg[41]
+ * and mcc reg[9] windows, at the same place as on the J713.
+ */
+&pmp_report {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &aop {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-1, DTV-AUD-2, DTV-AUD-13 */
 };
